**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The structural recoverability report: 'this kit can never recover X' and 'you need an off-axis cut', each with its remedy (001 §M 'It answers outright "this kit can never recover X" and "you need an off-axis cut"', 'Output: a recoverability report'; the S14.1 brief 'It outputs … findings'; specs/0044/.manual/004 §3.2 'Tilting alone is not sufficient'). In `MeasurementPlanner.fs`, after step 468's declarations, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S14.1. (1) `type SampleCut with member this.plateText : string`: `z-cut plate`, `x-cut plate`, `y-cut plate`, and for `TiltedCut a` `<a in degrees>° tilted-cut plate`. (2) `PlannerRemedy` = `AddPlateRemedy of SampleCut` | `ObliqueIncidenceRemedy of cap : Angle` | `FullMuellerRemedy`, with `member this.text : string`: `add one <plateText>`, `tilt a plate (its internal angle reaches at most <cap in degrees>°)` and `use a full Mueller polarimeter, or a polarizer and an analyzer around the plate`. (3) `TargetFinding = { target : CrystalComponent; reason : UnseenReason; remedies : PlannerRemedy list }`. (4) `OffAxisCutNeed = { targets : CrystalComponent list; capAngle : Angle; cuts : SampleCut list }`. (5) `PlannerFinding` = `UnrecoverableTargetFinding of TargetFinding | OffAxisCutFinding of OffAxisCutNeed`, with `member this.text : string`: `This kit can never recover <name>: <reason text>.` and `You need an off-axis cut: <the targets' names joined by ", "> lie along the normal of every plate, and a tilt carries the wave at most <capAngle in degrees>° off it; add <"one " + each cut's plateText, joined by " or ">.`. Every angle in a text is in degrees with one decimal, formatted under `CultureInfo.InvariantCulture`. (6) `RecoverabilityReport = { symmetry : CrystalSymmetry; reachable : CrystalComponent list; findings : PlannerFinding list }`, with `member this.unrecoverable : CrystalComponent list` (the targets of its `UnrecoverableTargetFinding`s, in order) and `member this.offAxisCutOpt : OffAxisCutNeed option`. (7) `PlannerError`, an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string`, with `UnknownPlannerTargetErr` and `member this.describe : string` rendering it `the crystal has no such parameter: <reason>`. (8) `type CrystalParameters with member this.structuralReport (targets : ParameterName list) (looks : PlannerLook list) : Result<RecoverabilityReport, PlannerError>`. (a) The first target name that no component of `this.components` (step 466) has answers `UnknownPlannerTargetErr` naming it and the crystal's names. (b) Each target component, in target order, goes by `targetSightOf looks` (step 468) into `reachable` or into an `UnrecoverableTargetFinding` of its reason and remedies. (c) The candidate plates are the crystal's distinct principal cuts, `[ ZCut; XCut ]` when `this.symmetry.anisotropy` is `Uniaxial` (a y-cut looks at a uniaxial crystal as an x-cut does, `MuellerInverse.fs:SampleCut`'s doc) and `[ ZCut; XCut; YCut ]` otherwise; a candidate SEES the component when the normal-incidence look `{ normalAxisOpt = cut.normalAxisOpt; incidence = IncidenceAngle.normal; observable = TransmittedMueller; reach = FullMuellerReach }` answers `SeenInLook`, and is MISSING when no look has its `normalAxisOpt`. Remedies by reason: `NoLookReason`, `AddPlateRemedy` of every candidate that sees the component, then `FullMuellerRemedy`; `AlongEveryPropagationReason` and `NoRetardanceReason`, `AddPlateRemedy` of every missing candidate that sees it, then `ObliqueIncidenceRemedy this.snellCap`; `NormalIncidenceOnlyReason`, `[ ObliqueIncidenceRemedy this.snellCap ]` alone, because more plates do not substitute for a tilt (`BiaxialInverseTests.fs:42-48`); `FullMuellerNeededReason`, `[ FullMuellerRemedy ]`. (d) When the looks are not empty and every look's `normalAxisOpt` is the same `Some a`, the targets whose component's `axes` is exactly `[ a ]`, in target order, give, if there are any, one `OffAxisCutFinding { targets; capAngle = this.snellCap; cuts = the candidates whose normalAxisOpt is not Some a }` after the target findings: every plate puts those components on its normal, so only a tilt reaches them, at most `snellCap` off it. (e) `symmetry` is `this.symmetry` (step 465). The report adds no caching and reads nothing beyond its arguments. Tests, in `PlannerReportTests`, over its probes: `each unrecoverable target names the missing plates and the tilt or the reach that would recover it`: over the normal z-cut look alone (transmitted, `FullMuellerReach`) the uniaxial report's `reachable` is [g11] and its target findings are n_o `NoRetardanceReason`, n_e and g33 `AlongEveryPropagationReason`, each with `[ AddPlateRemedy XCut; ObliqueIncidenceRemedy <the probe's snellCap> ]`; over a normal x-cut look under `EllipsometricReach` g11 and g33 are `FullMuellerNeededReason` with `[ FullMuellerRemedy ]`; the triclinic g12 over the three principal cuts at normal incidence has `[ ObliqueIncidenceRemedy <its snellCap> ]` alone; over no look the uniaxial g11 has `[ AddPlateRemedy ZCut; AddPlateRemedy XCut; FullMuellerRemedy ]`. `plates that all put the same axis on their normal call for an off-axis cut`: the uniaxial report over the normal z-cut look has `offAxisCutOpt = Some { targets = [ n_e; g33 ]; capAngle = <its snellCap>; cuts = [ XCut ] }` as its last finding; over that look and the same z-cut oblique it has no target finding and the same off-axis finding; over that look and a normal x-cut look it has no finding at all; the triclinic report over the normal z-cut look has the off-axis targets [ n3; g33 ] and cuts [ XCut; YCut ]. `a target the crystal does not have refuses the report, naming it`: the target name `n2` over the uniaxial probe answers `UnknownPlannerTargetErr` whose reason names `n2`, and its `describe` starts `the crystal has no such parameter: `. `the findings read as sentences naming the parameter, the reason and the remedy`: over the normal z-cut look the uniaxial report's findings read `This kit can never recover n_e: every look propagates along its axes.` and `You need an off-axis cut: n_e, g33 lie along the normal of every plate, and a tilt carries the wave at most 40.4° off it; add one x-cut plate.`, and its n_o remedies read `add one x-cut plate` and `tilt a plate (its internal angle reaches at most 40.4°)`.

**Acceptance.** After the report lands, `CrystalParameters.structuralReport` MUST answer the reachable targets, an unrecoverable-target finding with its reason and remedies for every other target, and an off-axis-cut finding when every plate puts a target's only axis on its normal, refusing an unknown target with `UnknownPlannerTargetErr`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `each unrecoverable target names the missing plates and the tilt or the reach that would recover it`, `plates that all put the same axis on their normal call for an off-axis cut`, `a target the crystal does not have refuses the report, naming it` and `the findings read as sentences naming the parameter, the reason and the remedy`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s45 invariants MUST pass.
